    "title": "What time does the Oscars red carpet start? How to watch",
    "text": "Updated March 15, 2026, 4:55 p.m. ETThe Oscars is one of the biggest nights in fashion, giving viewers a glimpse into what to expect from luxury fashion houses.The 98th Academy Awards take place Sunday, March 15. But before the best picture can be crowned, nominees will line the red carpet in gorgeous gowns and suits.This year will likely be different from recent Oscar ceremonies. Items from the archives have dominated the red carpet in the last couple years, as a slew of creative director changes stunted the showcase of new designs.Chanel, Dior, Valentino and Gucci all have different creative directors than last year, according to \"Vogue Business.\" Now, they're ready to make their mark.“For so many new creative directors, this is their moment to really show the world — not just the fashion community and the people at the shows — their new direction and make a statement,” luxury consultant Robert Burke told the online fashion industry publication.So, where can you see the looks? Here's how to watch the Oscars red carpet:When does the Oscars red carpet start?The official live red carpet show will air at 6:30 p.m. ET/3:30 p.m. PT. Pre-shows will begin even earlier. See the times below.Where to watch Oscars red carpet?The official red carpet show will air live on ABC and broadcast outlets and stream on Hulu. “Chicken Shop Date” star Amelia Dimoldenberg will host.Several stations will also air Oscars pre-coverage. ABC News and ABC-owned television stations will present a star-studded preshow, \"On the Red Carpet at the Oscars,\" at 3:30 p.m. ET/12:30 p.m. PT. Lara Spencer, along with Whit Johnson and Linsey Davis, will interview this year’s Oscar nominees and presenters alongside George Pennacchio, Joelle Garguilo and Chris Connelly.E!'s red carpet coverage – \"Live From E!: Oscars 2026\" − will air live on the network and will also simulcast on Peacock. Coverage starts at 4 p.m. ET/1 p.m. PT with Zuri Hall hosting.Oscars red carpet livestreamYou can stream the Oscars red carpet show on Hulu or any streaming service that carries ABC, such as YouTube TV or Fubo.What time are the Oscars tonight?The awards ceremony is scheduled to commence at 7 p.m. ET/4 p.m. PT.What channel is the Oscars on 2026?The 2026 Oscars will air live on ABC and the ABC app (if you're a cable subscriber) on Sunday at 7 p.m./4 p.m. PT.You can also stream the awards ceremony live on Hulu and via Fubo.",
